    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and favorable handedness, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from an elite leadoff spot against Phillips; his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the opportunity to exploit a shaky 4.51 xERA make him the engine of our SB-chasing strategy. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** is locked in as a high-floor start, as his +13% platoon edge against Singer provides the necessary efficiency boost to overcome standard variance. While **Yordan Alvarez** (68.04) faces a tough L/L matchup, his elite 0.450 xwOBA forces him into the starting lineup despite the inherent regression risk of hitting against Rodriguez.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Colt Keith** (45.59), who ultimately fell to the bench. While **Colt Keith** narrowly missed our starting cut, the combination of a daunting 2.89 xERA from Williams and a significant -19% penalty for opposing pitcher skill made him a less attractive option than the mid-order production we anticipate from **Caleb Durbin** (65.89). We also remain cautious with **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (55.65); despite a park boost, the 3.44 xERA of Tolle suggests a tighter margin for error. We are monitoring **Kazuma Okamoto** (59.79) and **Junior Caminero** (59.63) closely, as both are hovering near our \"Marginal\" threshold\u2014if any late weather reports shift in favor of the pitchers, we will have to weigh the risk of depleting our game caps against their slightly elevated projections. **Gary Sanchez**, **Carson Benge**, and **Dillon Dingler** remain stashed to preserve our season-long caps, as none currently meet our 40.0 efficiency floor requirement for active play.",
